3. State Variables, Controls, and Exogenous Forcings

Time is discrete, indexed annually by t.

3.1 State Variables

Variable Meaning Units
E_t Installed dispatchable electricity generation capacity TWh/year maximum output
K_{c,t} AI compute capacity ExaFLOP/s
D_t Usable AI training data stock Index, [0,1]
A_t AI capability index Index, [0,1]
H_t Average human capability index Index, [0,1]
L_t Labor force Millions of workers
S_t Scientific knowledge stock Index, [0,1]
I_t Physical infrastructure stock Index, [0,1]
R_t Resilience stock Index, [0,1]
F_t Freedom index Index, [0,1], V-Dem Liberal Democracy Index
X_t Extraterrestrial autonomy index Index, [0,1]
K_t Non-AI physical capital stock Trillions of constant USD
Z_t Total factor productivity Index, positive

Correction from v0.3: H_{AI,t} is not a state variable. It is a semi-endogenous forcing, estimated from corporate compute concentration data. It is listed in Section 3.4 below.

3.2 Control Variables

Controls are annual investment expenditures in constant dollars:

u_t = (u_{E,t}, u_{Kc,t}, u_{H,t}, u_{S,t}, u_{I,t}, u_{R,t}, u_{F,t}, u_{X,t})

All controls are nonnegative.

3.3 Budget Constraint

The admissible control set is:

\sum_{i \in \mathcal{C}} u_{i,t} \le \tau Y_t + G_t

where

\mathcal{C} = \{E, Kc, H, S, I, R, F, X\}

· \tau \in (0,1) is the maximum share of output that can be allocated to these investments,
· G_t is exogenous public investment support.

Without this constraint, the viability kernel is trivial: a planner could invest infinite resources in every state.

3.4 Exogenous and Semi-Endogenous Forcings

The following are treated as exogenous or semi-endogenous:

· n_t: labor force growth rate.
· G_t: public R&D and infrastructure funding.
· H_{AI,t}: Herfindahl index of frontier AI compute ownership. This is semi-endogenous: it depends on K_{c,t} and corporate concentration data. In the current draft, it is treated as an exogenous forcing for estimation simplicity.
· E_{base,t}: non-AI electricity demand.

For preliminary estimation, H_{AI,t} is modeled as:

H_{AI,t} = h(K_{c,t}, \text{ownership concentration}_t)

where h(\cdot) is estimated from EPOCH AI ownership data and SEC 10-K GPU asset disclosures.

