7. Research Hypotheses

7.1 H1: AI Augmentation

Let \theta_1 - \theta_2 be the net effect of AI capability on human capability.

H_0: \theta_1 - \theta_2 \le 0

H_1: \theta_1 - \theta_2 > 0

In production terms, H1 also implies that the human labor income share s_{H,t} does not collapse as A_t rises under appropriate institutions.

7.2 H2: Democratic Adaptation

Let \tau be the number of years required for GDP per capita to return to its pre-shock trend after a major technological or macroeconomic shock.

H_0: \tau_{\text{democ}} \ge \tau_{\text{non-democ}}

H_1: \tau_{\text{democ}} < \tau_{\text{non-democ}}

7.3 H3: Space Feedback

The space-spillover parameter \gamma_{\text{space}} is split into two channels:

\gamma_{\text{space}} = \gamma_{\text{launch}} + \gamma_{\text{science}}

· \gamma_{\text{launch}}: TFP spillover from launch-cost reduction, measurable via the price per kilogram to LEO. This channel is expected to be positive due to downstream IT and communication applications.
· \gamma_{\text{science}}: TFP spillover from NASA science and technology transfer, measurable via patent citation networks and NASA Tech Transfer data.

The hypotheses are stated separately:

H_3^{\text{launch}}: \gamma_{\text{launch}} > 0

H_3^{\text{science}}: \gamma_{\text{science}} > 0.5 \gamma_{\text{terrestrial}}

where \gamma_{\text{terrestrial}} is the TFP elasticity from comparable terrestrial frontier R&D (e.g., NSF or DOE programs).

Critical engagement with Kantor & Whalley (2025): Kantor and Whalley find that space-race federal R&D produced localized gains in manufacturing value added, employment, and capital accumulation in space-related sectors, but limited evidence of economy-wide TFP spillovers. This suggests that \gamma_{\text{science}} may be small relative to \gamma_{\text{terrestrial}}. The pre-registered threshold is set accordingly: if \gamma_{\text{science}} \le 0.5 \gamma_{\text{terrestrial}}, H3-science is rejected. The model does not require H3-science to be true. If it is false, space investment is still justified for direct strategic and civilizational reasons, but not as a broad TFP spillover mechanism.

7.4 H4: Multiplanetary Risk Reduction — Model-Internal Sensitivity Analysis

Let P_{ext}(X) be the modeled extinction probability at extraterrestrial autonomy level X.

This hypothesis is not empirical in the same sense as H1–H3, because P_{ext} is never directly observed. It is a model-internal sensitivity analysis. It is therefore placed in this separate subsection rather than numbered as an empirical claim.

H_4: \frac{P_{ext}(0.3) - P_{ext}(0)}{P_{ext}(0)} < -0.5

This is a simulation-based hypothesis. If increasing X from 0 to 0.3 does not reduce median modeled P_{ext} by at least 50%, H4 is rejected within the model.

