8. Empirical Strategy

8.1 Identifiability Statement

The full structural system in Section 4 contains more than forty free parameters. The available U.S. annual data on frontier AI compute spans roughly 2012–2025—at most 10–15 usable observations. Joint estimation of the full system is not feasible. Therefore, the structural system is calibrated from literature-sourced elasticities (Acemoglu & Restrepo, Hoffmann et al., EPOCH, IEA, V-Dem), not jointly estimated.

The four hypotheses H1–H4 are validated through reduced-form designs, not through a full-system GMM or Bayesian fit. The reduced-form tests are:

· H1: industry-level difference-in-differences across high- vs. low-AI-exposure U.S. industries.
· H2: matched cross-country recovery-time comparisons.
· H3: patent/citation-based comparison of space-directed R&D vs. terrestrial frontier R&D.
· H4: model-internal simulation ensembles.

This distinction is essential: the structural model is a coherence device, not an estimation engine.

