8.3 Identification Strategy

The United States offers useful subnational variation:

· States with different AI data center investments.
· Industries with different AI exposure by task composition.
· Regions with different energy mixes.
· University clusters with differential access to the National AI Research Resource pilot.

These allow difference-in-differences and synthetic control designs.

Treatment definition for state-level DiD:

· Treated: states receiving >1 GW of new AI data center capacity and NAIRR Pilot access.
· Control: synthetic control matched on industrial composition, energy mix, and baseline human capability.

