9. Operational Falsification Criteria

All thresholds should be preregistered before confirmatory analysis.

F1. AI Does Not Reduce Aggregate Human Capability

Measure: The elasticity of human capability with respect to AI capability,

\frac{d \ln H_t}{d \ln A_t}

estimated in a panel over four-year windows.

Data: BLS O*NET AI exposure scores, Eloundou et al. (2024) exposure scores, Gmyrek et al. (2025) automation/augmentation scores, Anthropic Economic Index.

Design: Difference-in-differences across high-AI-exposure and low-AI-exposure U.S. industries.

Rejection threshold: If top-quartile AI-exposure industries show a relative decline in human value-added per worker of more than 2% per year after 2026, and the observed automation share exceeds 30% of tasks in those industries, H1 is rejected.

Note on aggregate vs. sectoral: This test is sectoral. To avoid rejecting H1 when aggregate human capability rises through reallocation, a second preregistered test uses an aggregate measure of H_t (PIAAC scores, labor productivity, task complexity indices) and requires a positive aggregate elasticity.

F2. Democratic Adaptation Is Not Inferior

Measure: Recovery time \tau to return to pre-shock GDP per capita trend.

Data: V-Dem, IMF crisis recovery databases, World Bank indicators.

Design: Matched democratic and non-democratic cases.

Rejection threshold: If democracies do not recover at least one year faster than matched non-democracies at the 95% confidence level, H2 is rejected.

F3. Space Investment Generates Innovation Feedback

Measure: Two channels:

\gamma_{\text{launch}}, \quad \gamma_{\text{science}}

with lags of 7–10 years.

Data: NASA Tech Transfer, USPTO patents, citation networks, comparable NSF and DOE programs, launch cost per kg to LEO.

Design: Comparison of space-directed R&D with terrestrial frontier R&D.

Rejection thresholds:

· \gamma_{\text{launch}} is rejected if \gamma_{\text{launch}} \le 0.
· \gamma_{\text{science}} is rejected if \gamma_{\text{science}} \le 0 or \gamma_{\text{science}} < 0.5 \gamma_{\text{terrestrial}} over ten years.

Based on Kantor and Whalley (2025), the science channel is expected to be rejected. That is a falsification-oriented outcome, not a problem for the framework.

F4. Extraterrestrial Autonomy Lowers Extinction Risk — Model-Internal

Measure: Modeled P_{ext} under X=0 versus X=0.3.

Data: Simulation ensembles, expert elicitation, NASA risk models.

Design: Counterfactual modeling with explicit uncertainty intervals.

Rejection threshold: If increasing X from 0 to 0.3 does not reduce median modeled P_{ext} by at least 50%, H4 is rejected within the model.

