10. Roadmap Stages with Objective Metrics

Stage Objective Metric Failure Mode
I. AI Adaptation AAI_t > 1 over 4-year windows AI productivity rises while human capability declines
II. Energy and Compute Abundance EIE_t = \frac{\text{cognitive output}}{\text{AI electricity demand}} increases Compute growth slows due to energy bottlenecks and grid queues
III. Human Capital Regeneration PIAAC score growth, labor force participation Education system fails to adapt within 12–16 years
IV. Industrial Autonomy Manufacturing TFP growth Automation does not translate into broad industrial capacity
V. Lunar Civilization Infrastructure EAI_{\text{Moon}} > 0.2 Lunar node remains Earth-dependent
VI. Martian Civilization EAI_{\text{Mars}} > 0.4 Mars remains a scientific outpost
VII. Multiplanetary Civilization MRI = 1 - P_{ext}^{\text{multi}} increases Multiple nodes do not reduce system extinction risk

The extraterrestrial autonomy index EAI is defined as:

EAI = w_E \cdot \text{power closure} + w_L \cdot \text{ECLSS closure} + w_M \cdot \text{propellant closure}

with weights summing to unity.

